{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MkkVcNxJPnM35KqSmju26k","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"metadata\": {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n     4→    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n     5→    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n     6→    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n     7→    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n     8→    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n     9→    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    10→    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n    11→  },\n    12→  \"structure\": [\n    13→    {\n    14→      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n    15→      \"title\": null,\n    16→      \"index\": 1,\n    17→      \"start_position\": 28,\n    18→      \"end_position\": 13811,\n    19→      \"word_count\": 2443,\n    20→      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    21→      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    22→      \"children\": [],\n    23→      \"characters_present\": [\n    24→        \"Prince Prospero\",\n    25→        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n    26→        \"The courtiers\",\n    27→        \"Musicians\",\n    28→        \"Buffoons\",\n    29→        \"Improvisatori\",\n    30→        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n    31→        \"Beauty\"\n    32→      ],\n    33→      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastation of the Red Death across the land, a plague marked by bloody pores and swift death, prompting Prince Prospero to retreat with a thousand courtiers into his sealed, opulent abbey to escape contagion. Inside, seven uniquely colored rooms—each with stained-glass windows matching their decor, except the final black chamber with blood-red panes—host a lavish masked ball, illuminated only by firelight from external tripods. As the night progresses, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber, where the figure is found to be empty, revealing the Red Death has infiltrated even their sanctuary. The plague then claims every reveller, the clock stops, the lights die, and darkness and decay reign supreme.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"Prospero\",\n    42→        \"the mummer\"\n    43→      ],\n    44→      \"role\": null,\n    45→      \"appearance\": null,\n    46→      \"personality\": null,\n    47→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    48→      \"descriptions\": [\n    49→        {\n    50→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a noble figure who retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to escape the Red Death, hosting a lavish masked ball during the height of the plague. He exhibits a shift from confidence and authority to rage and desperation when confronted by a masked figure resembling the Red Death, ultimately dying upon contact with the intruder in the black chamber.\",\n    51→          \"source_position\": 1894,\n    52→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    53→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    54→        }\n    55→      ],\n    56→      \"relationships\": {},\n    57→      \"evidence\": [\n    58→        {\n    59→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to avoid the Red Death\",\n    60→          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero seals himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to avoid the plague\",\n    61→          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n    62→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    63→        },\n    64→        {\n    65→          \"statement\": \"He hosts a lavish masked ball during the plague\",\n