ysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber, where the figure is found to be empty, revealing the Red Death has infiltrated even their sanctuary. The plague then claims every reveller, the clock stops, the lights die, and darkness and decay reign supreme.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\",\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a noble figure who retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to escape the Red Death, hosting a lavish masked ball during the height of the plague. He exhibits a shift from confidence and authority to rage and desperation when confronted by a masked figure resembling the Red Death, ultimately dying upon contact with the intruder in the black chamber.\",\n          \"source_position\": 1894,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero retreats with a thousand courtiers into a sealed abbey to avoid the Red Death\",\n          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero seals himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to avoid the plague\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He hosts a lavish masked ball during the plague\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was toward the close of the fifth or sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad, that the Prince Prospero entertained his thousand friends at a masked ball of the most unusual magnificence.\",\n          \"position\": 1894,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He reacts with rage and demands the masked figure be unmasked and hanged\",\n          \"quote\": \"Insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He pursues the masked figure through all seven rooms with a dagger\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had...\",\n          \"position\": 12389,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He dies instantly upon confronting the masked figure in the black chamber\",\n          \"quote\": \"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero.\",\n          \"position\": 12980,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pronunciations\": [\n    {\n      \"word\": \"Prospero\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n      \"occurrences\": 18,\n      \"first_position\": 631,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...izure, progress and termination of the disease, were the incidents